            <title>[LU-21131] TCU: hard link from .Trash into the namespace is allowed, bypassing unrm/ownership checks</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21131</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;h2&gt;&lt;a name="Problem"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Problem&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A file that has been deleted into the Trash Can can be hard-linked back into the normal namespace:&lt;br/&gt;
 &lt;tt&gt;mkdir /mnt/lustre/d; echo x &amp;gt; /mnt/lustre/d/f; rm /mnt/lustre/d/fln /mnt/lustre/d/.Trash/f /mnt/lustre/d/x      # succeeds&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
The object now has a live namespace name, but it still carries &lt;tt&gt;LUSTRE_UNRM_FL&lt;/tt&gt;, the &lt;tt&gt;trusted.unrm&lt;/tt&gt; xattr and the trash uid/gid/projid. As a result:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;it bypasses &lt;tt&gt;lfs trash unrm&lt;/tt&gt;, so the original owner and ids are never restored and quota stays charged to the trash projid;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;the object is still listed in &lt;tt&gt;.Trash&lt;/tt&gt;, so &lt;tt&gt;ltrash_purge&lt;/tt&gt; or &lt;tt&gt;lfs trash clean&lt;/tt&gt; will unlink the trash name while the namespace link survives. That leaves a file with the UNRM flag and trash ownership in the namespace;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;depending on directory permissions, a user other than the owner can create the link. This is related to the authorization gap in EX-16344.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;h2&gt;&lt;a name="Expected"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Expected&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;tt&gt;link(2)&lt;/tt&gt; with a source inside &lt;tt&gt;.Trash&lt;/tt&gt; or &lt;tt&gt;.lustre/.ltrash&lt;/tt&gt;, or a source with &lt;tt&gt;LUSTRE_UNRM_FL&lt;/tt&gt;, should fail with EPERM or EXDEV. The MDT should enforce this in &lt;tt&gt;mdt_reint_link&lt;/tt&gt; / &lt;tt&gt;mdd_link_sanity_check&lt;/tt&gt;, not only the client.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
